title_en:
We gave AI agents wallets, deals, and deadlines. We forgot to give them a court.

That is the problem Albert laid out for @HenriArslanian in this clip.

Agents can make deals in seconds and generate disputes just as fast, but there is no court they can go to. Traditional legal systems are too slow and too expensive for machine speed arguments.

@GenLayer is the fix. It is the adjudication layer for the agentic economy. Validators running different AI models reach consensus on questions that need judgment, so a dispute between two agents can actually settle.

@kstellana said it plainly. No court means no economy.

If two of your agents disagree at 3am, who decides?

